The Solana NFT and TCG scene kept moving around Breakpoint 2026, with physical trading cards landing in London and established collections staying active through side events and community presence.

A quick look at some of what’s been moving with #SolanaRecap

@Collector_Crypt brought the Solana Base Set to Breakpoint. These are real physical trading cards featuring 35 Solana projects, manufactured by Orange Cap Games and sponsored by the Solana Foundation. Attendees were able to rip packs on site in London. The team also launched their mobile app just ahead of the event and has shared that pack sales have reached $1.5 billion. Their CEO spoke on stage about the role of nostalgia in collecting.

@Beezie announced a partnership with Collector Crypt at Breakpoint. The collaboration pairs Beezie’s digital claw machine and luxury collectibles audience with Collector Crypt’s trading card infrastructure and distribution. Beezie also introduced Mia, a discovery shopping experience built for women. The move is framed as expanding the overall on-chain collectibles market rather than pure competition.

@Claynosaurz had a visible presence throughout Breakpoint. The team thanked everyone who stopped by their space and connected in person. They also ran light activations, including plushie giveaways with Superteam Malaysia, and were finalists in the Breakpoint 2026 Community Awards in both the Solana NFT Community and Collab of the Year categories. The collection continues building out its character brand and animation efforts alongside the core NFT community.

@MadLads remained part of the conversation around the event. Holders and community members noted the collection’s art and presence during Breakpoint side activities, including a joint evening with Claynosaurz. The project continues as one of the more established PFP collections on Solana.

@SolanaMBS / MonkeDAO showed up in force in London. Over 330 Monkes were in town for Breakpoint, with multiple community events including a Fog & Fortune activation with @RedotPay, Rise & Shine Yoga, exclusive MNKD drops tied to MonkeHotel stays, and travel guides put out ahead of the week. The team published The Banana Split #248 covering the London takeover. It was a strong holder meetup and side-event week rather than a new product drop.

@BoredApeYC / @yugalabs Mudwater continues to see activity on Solana. The first set (Swamp Origins) features 120 card designs with foil, serialized, and cracked-ice variants. Each pack contains 10 cards and is backed by a printed version held in a vault. BAYC holders can claim 10 packs and MAYC holders can claim 2, with the claim window open through January 19, 2027. Packs and individual cards are tradable as Solana NFTs, with opening available on the official site. The team has also been running Whatnot streams and tying fresh packs into IRL gift-swap meetups.

@crittersquest runs an on-chain 4X strategy game on Solana where players use Master Edition and Clone NFTs to build, gather, craft, and raid. Season 2 (Oct 8 – Nov 8) added competitive world events such as the World Bank, where players kill a guardian, race for shards, and try to hold the seat for rewards. Season 3 starts December 18 and introduces Titans (Floranix, Terravus, Axiom, Aquaris, Chronos, Solus, Necrothis) as large map bosses that require squads to defeat and split the spoils. Players are currently in a gather phase stocking up for the new season.

@misfitsorder continues shipping utility for its 5,000-supply collection on Solana. The project started as a free mint and has since rolled out tools for holders, The Misfits Lab for on-chain trait swapping, and a staking model that pays in SOL. Around Breakpoint the team teased limited-time Grand Theft NFT traits (Mason or Lumia) and noted Lab doors opening, while keeping the focus on holder tools rather than pure speculation.

